    {
      "block_id": "2605.28896_p2_b18",
      "text": "The superposition hypothesis [Elhage et al., 2022] posits that neural networks encode more\nfeatures than they have dimensions by representing features as nearly-orthogonal directions,\nallowing superposition of many sparse features. SAEs provide a practical tool to decompose this\n",
